WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.142
Hi! Who are you?

2
00:00:09.143 --> 00:00:14.750
I'm a red-eyed tree frog.

3
00:00:14.751 --> 00:00:19.990
Frogs are amphibians.

4
00:00:19.991 --> 00:00:22.966
Where do you live?

5
00:00:22.967 --> 00:00:29.665
Red-eyed tree frogs live in North and South America.

6
00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:33.899
We like rain forests.

7
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:37.358
Do you live in trees?

8
00:00:37.359 --> 00:00:42.219
We live in trees near water.

9
00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:46.538
Tadpoles live in the water.

10
00:00:46.539 --> 00:00:51.049
Tadpoles are baby frogs.

11
00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.844
What do you eat?

12
00:00:53.845 --> 00:00:59.035
Red-eyed tree frogs eat insects.

13
00:00:59.036 --> 00:01:05.007
We like crickets, moths, and flies.

14
00:01:05.008 --> 00:01:17.422
We catch prey with our long, sticky tongues.

15
00:01:17.423 --> 00:01:20.132
Where do you sleep?

16
00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:25.770
We sleep on the bottoms of leaves.

17
00:01:25.771 --> 00:01:30.545
We can stick to the leaves!

18
00:01:30.546 --> 00:01:35.828
Do you have any enemies?

19
00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:41.121
Birds and snakes try to eat us.

20
00:01:41.122 --> 00:01:46.062
But our colors help protect us.

21
00:01:46.063 --> 00:01:56.180
Our green bodies blend in with leaves.

22
00:01:56.181 --> 00:02:01.738
What if an enemy sees you?

23
00:02:01.739 --> 00:02:07.156
Our red eyes can surprise enemies.

24
00:02:07.157 --> 00:02:10.456
Then we jump!

25
00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:19.496
Our orange legs also surprise enemies.

26
00:02:19.497 --> 00:02:24.363
Oh no! I see a snake!

27
00:02:24.364 --> 00:02:32.472
Good-bye, Red-eyed Tree Frog!

